~ start
Mister Dam: [#dynamic_portrait=MisterDamPortrait]Hellooooooo. Come to join my gameeeee?
do GameManager.give_name_note("mister_dam")
- Can I ask about the rules first?
	Mister Dam: [do portrait_with_part.assign_part(true)]Rules, rules, rules... Of course you can.
	~ explain_rule
	Mister Dam: [do portrait_with_part.assign_part(true)]We will play a shooting game. Here're the rules:
	Mister Dam: [do portrait_with_part.assign_part(false)][color=yellow]Rule 1[/color]: Use WASD, not the arrow key, to aim your crosshair.
	Mister Dam: [do portrait_with_part.assign_part(true)][color=yellow]Rule 2[/color]: Use Space button to shoot.
	Mister Dam: [do portrait_with_part.assign_part(true)][color=yellow]Rule 3[/color]: Shoot all the cans before the time run out to win.
	Mister Dam: [do portrait_with_part.assign_part(false)][color=yellow]Rule 4[/color]: The crosshair move up when you press the up button, and vice versa.
	do GameManager.give_rule_paper("mister_dam")
	Mister Dam: I hope you remember the rules and not ask me again.
	- I'm not. Care to speak again?
		Mister Dam: [do portrait_with_part.assign_part(true)][shake]Listen here this sleepy guy[/shake]:
		=> explain_rule
	- I got the rule, let me play.
		=> play_game
	- Yeah, but I don't wanna play anymore.
		Mister Dam: [do portrait_with_part.assign_part(true)]Suit yourself.
		=> END
- Yes, please!
	~ play_game
	Mister Dam: [do portrait_with_part.assign_part(true)]Very good. I will prepare the game for you to play!
	do GameManager.map_manager.start_minigame("shoot_can")
	if GameManager.last_minigame_won
		Mister Dam: [do portrait_with_part.assign_part(true)]Wow, didn't think you would win. Very good!
	else
		Mister Dam: [do portrait_with_part.assign_part(true)]Better luck next time!
	=> END
- No
	=> END
=> END